@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] shared-domain-has-one-implementation
Review, search, motion and AI policies extracted into this module MUST have one
production implementation consumed by Android and iOS. The shared domain MUST NOT
depend on Android, Compose or native UI services. Existing Android packages MUST remain
available through the `android/core` compatibility facade. Source: Tavi, 21 Oct 2026, choosing Compose
Multiplatform with maximum reuse for the iOS mode.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:motion;architecture] shared-page-way-follows-the-finger
`pageWay` MUST derive forward or backward from page order. `swipeStep` MUST count a
throw in the direction of the drag even when the drag is short, and a throw against
the drag MUST cancel it. Native callers supply their release threshold; the app's
500dp/s threshold remains defined by `android/DESIGN.md` rule 105.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] shared-path-keeps-whole-tail
A shortened path MUST keep its end and drop whole folders from the front, never cut a
name in the middle (`android/DESIGN.md` rule 90).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] shared-review-next-unreviewed
After a file is marked reviewed, the next-file policy MUST choose the next unreviewed
file in order, wrapping to the beginning when needed. It MUST return no next file
when every other file is reviewed or the current file is absent from the order.
Source: `android/DESIGN.md` rule 65; F55; existing `nextUnreviewed` behavior retained
by Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 shared-code decision.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] shared-code-zoom-keeps-the-point
The code-zoom arithmetic MUST keep the point under the fingers at its screen position
as code is laid out at its new text size. Notes and threads MUST retain their own size,
and horizontal scroll MUST NOT go before the content's start. Source: recording
16 Oct 09:50, 04:11 to 04:26 (M9), and 15 Oct 15:37, 09:58 to 10:11 (L17), as cited by
`diff-pinch-keeps-the-line` in the review contracts.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] shared-work-notice-server-time
The ongoing AI work summary MUST include only running whole-diff work and MUST use the
oldest running task's server start time for elapsed time. A missing or future start
MUST omit elapsed time. Terminal tasks MUST disappear independently when other tasks
still run. Source: Tavi's 20 Oct request to explore app notifications for ongoing AI
work; the existing `core-work-notice-real-time` behavior is shared unchanged.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-ai-outcome-owned-task
AI outcome alerts MUST match an explicitly persisted task ID, key and kind. Only
authoritative done or failed statuses MAY alert; cancelled settles silently, and
missing, unknown or network interruption MUST NOT imply an outcome. Expired ownership
MUST NOT produce a late alert. Source: Tavi, 21 Oct 2026, notification expansion; the
existing `core-ai-result-alerts-require-explicit-owned-task` policy is shared unchanged.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] shared-brief-is-inert-data
A brief MUST be parsed from the server's plain `{type, props}` tree into known native
blocks. It MUST NOT execute the tree, and a component the app does not know MUST NOT
be drawn. Source: architecture, The brief; the `ai-brief-is-data` contract and parser
are retained by Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 shared-code decision.
